<title>USA: FCC pegs US corn crop at 9.33 bln bu, soy 2.37 bln.</title>
<headline>FCC pegs US corn crop at 9.33 bln bu, soy 2.37 bln.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farmers Commodities Corp said on Monday it estimated 1996/97 U.S. corn production at 9.330 billion bushels and soybean output at 2.369 billion.</p>
<p>FCC estimated the U.S. corn yield at 127.33 bushels per acre and U.S. soybean yield at 37.34 bushels.</p>
<p>The U.S. Department of Agriculture on October 11 put U.S. corn output at 9.012 billion and the soybean crop at 2.346 billion. USDA forecast a corn yield of 123.0 bushels and soybean yield of 37.0 bushels.</p>
<p>A month ago FCC put the U.S. corn crop at 9.078 billion and soybean production at 2.303 billion.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720</p>
</text>
